      "batch_node": {
        "source": "plugins.zizmor.grift.pages",
        "name": "zizmor Pages v0.6.0",
        "description": "Seeds /zizmor (about, findings, coverage, runs) and /zizmor/finding — one finding in full, reached from any audit cell on the findings table. See req-zizmor-page-landing and req-zizmor-page-finding. v0.3.0 (zizmor-tap#31): the findings table's badges actually render — tone maps for severity and confidence (Low only), datetime formatters on both timestamps, the stray column-level capitalize gone; /zizmor/finding leaves the navigation (it needs ?finding_id=); the finding-detail panel gains workflow_page_template, /github_core/workflow?workflow_id={workflow_id}, the key that page takes since tap-plugin-github-core#101. Panel and page node upserts; every id stable, batch id moved. v0.4.0 (zizmor-tap#33): the workflow page — /zizmor/workflow?workflow_id=… — one file, every finding on it: the annotated source with call-outs in the right margin (zizmor-workflow-source), then the same findings as a table over a per-workflow search (envelope mode, workflow_id typed integer). Not discoverable. One page, two panels, one search, three edges; every prior id stable. v0.5.0 (George): the workflow page is the annotated source alone — the findings table beneath it repeated the margin; the per-workflow search stays for consumers to bind. Panel node dropped from the bundle (an operator deletes it on a grid that has it; a shipped bundle cannot say 'gone'). Also v0.5.0: the workflow page carries github_core's anatomy graph beneath the file (edge to github_core's panel); the landing findings table's rows open the finding, its Workflow column opens the annotated file (via location.workflow_id, recorded by the collector from this version on) and a Repository column is added. v0.6.0: the finding page is three mounts — head, github_core's anatomy graph, body — and takes ?workflow_id= too; the landing table's links into it carry it."
      },
